l reports the reviewed commit, cause, both bar values for another-bar refusal, both digests for a test-set mismatch or both values for a tree or parent mismatch, and the attest step with the lane and round test list; it writes no brief and returns the refusal result. A successful render reports the attested commit and digest. The search reads the record and never runs the bar.\""," rationale = \"One shared record reader keeps each review route from assigning its own meaning to a verified review result. Searching only through record-only ancestors preserves a valid result across review bookkeeping while stopping at work that can invalidate it; refusing rather than re-running preserves the separation between recording a result and deciding whether it is usable.\""," test_refs = \"TC-371\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-957\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1913,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1913,"newLines":6,"lines":[" acceptance_criteria = \"A requested review renders when its commit carries a verified review record for the named test set, and when only record changes or no changes separate it from such a commit; it refuses without a brief when that record is absent, malformed, names another tree or parent, names another bar or test set, or when a commit above it changes a non-record path. Every refusal names the reviewed commit, the cause and the step that records a passing review bar; a test-set mismatch names both digests and a tree or parent mismatch names both values.\""," priority = \"S\""," verification = \"Test\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," aspect = \"process\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-957\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3666,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3666,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"Review rendering refuses with no brief for every absen